# bitcoinix revoked release signing keys: one ssh public key per line
# ("keytype keydata [comment]"), as read by `ssh-keygen -Y verify -r`.
#
# A key listed here is rejected for every tag it signed, whatever date the tag
# claims. Use this for a COMPROMISED key. For a key that is only retired, append
# valid-before="YYYYMMDD" to its line in ssh-allowed-signers instead: that check
# uses the tag's own date, which the key holder chooses, so it does not stop a
# compromised key. See SECURITY.md.
#
# Keep a revoked key's line in ssh-allowed-signers too; test/release-keys-test.sh
# checks that every key here is also listed there.
#
# helper/fetch-release.sh refuses to run without this file, because git only warns
# about a missing revocation file and then accepts the signature.
